  "name": "Spotted Seals (Phoca largha) in Alaska",
  "description": "Aerial surveys were flown in spring and summer (April, June and August 1992; September 1993) along the West Coast of Alaska from Cape Newenham to Pt Barrow, including Nunivak and St. Lawrence Islands.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To count hauled out seals on coastal areas of western Alaska north of Bristol Bay",
